Package: aragami
Version: @VERSION@
Section: utils
Priority: optional
Architecture: all
Depends: nodejs (>= 18)
Maintainer: Nesarf <Nesarf@users.noreply.github.com>
Homepage: https://github.com/Nesarf/Aragami
Description: static posture audit for Tor Browser and Firefox
 Aragami reads a browser install or profile and reports configuration posture and
 static residue across five layers: build, transport, content/authorization,
 metadata and endpoint.
 .
 It is read-only. It never launches the browser under audit and never uses the
 network except for the version lookup. Every response carries a boundary notice
 stating what the audit does not cover, because a clean audit is not proof of
 safety, and content encryption does not address the metadata layer at all.
